From: iOSPlus10 GPU-recovery agent
Subject: [PATCH] negroni cpu: PSCI CPU_SUSPEND idle states (0288)

Before: an idle core ran cpu_idle() -> WFI only (clock gating; the core and its caches
stay powered). Now, with negronicpuidle=1 (kernel default 0 = WFI only), a core whose
next timer deadline is at least the DT residency away calls PSCI CPU_SUSPEND with the DT
param (out/live.dts idle-states: silver-c4/gold-c4 "rail-pc" 0x40000004, residency 4090 /
4791 us); negronicpuidle=2 adds the cluster states (cluster-d4 l3-off 0x41000044 at >= 5309
us, cluster-e3 llcc-off 0x4100c344 at >= 13959 us) in platform-coordinated mode.

- PSCI probe at start: VERSION, FEATURES(CPU_SUSPEND) (extended StateID required),
  FEATURES(SET_SUSPEND_MODE); PC mode is kept (Linux psci_1_0_init default).
- Entry point negroni_secondary_entry (the CPU_ON entry) -> reset vector ->
  resume_idle_cpu (already every core's reset handler) -> arm_init_idle_cpu ->
  cpu_idle_exit(TRUE) -> negroni_cpuidle_resume(): PE_init_cpu (GIC redistributor
  and CPU interface) and setPop(rtcPop) (the timer's compare value).
- local-timer-stop: the earliest wake time of the cores that are down goes into the
  memory-mapped timer frame 0 (0x17421000, CNTP, SPI 8 = INTID 40, routed by IROUTER
  to that core); its IRQ IPIs every core whose time came (Linux tick broadcast).
- Guard: 3 power-downs in a row shorter than the residency -> 8 WFI idles.
- Log: "NEGRONI CPUIDLE: ..." at start, every 60 s per core and state
  "NEGRONI CPUIDLE: cpuN state S param 0x... entered N times: resumed, returned,
  denied, short, down ms (%), bcast wakes".
Boot-args: negronicpuidle (0/1/2), negronicpuidle_mask (0xff), negronicpuidle_bcast (1).

